    "originalText": "2.2 Professional Goals\nTeaching Channel’s coaching tools support personalized professional growth by giving educators a dedicated space to reflect on their practice, receive meaningful feedback, and set individual learning goals. Educators can upload videos of their own instruction, reflect on their strengths and areas for growth, and share videos with coaches, mentors, or peers for feedback. Time-stamped comments can be aligned to state or district instructional frameworks, helping connect feedback and reflection to established professional expectations. Through this ongoing cycle of self-reflection, targeted feedback, and goal setting, educators can identify areas for improvement and monitor their progress toward meaningful professional learning goals.\nSet a personalized growth goal, upload a classroom video, and reflect on specific moments of instruction using your state or district framework.",
    "revisedText": "2.2 Professional Goals\nTeaching Channel’s coaching tools support personalized professional growth by giving educators a dedicated space to reflect on their practice, receive meaningful feedback, and set individual learning goals. Educators can upload videos of their own instruction, reflect on their strengths and areas for growth, and share videos with coaches, mentors, or peers for feedback. Time-stamped comments can be aligned to state or district instructional frameworks, helping connect feedback and reflection to established professional expectations. Through this ongoing cycle of self-reflection, targeted feedback, and goal setting, educators can identify areas for improvement and monitor their progress toward meaningful professional learning goals.\n\n\nSet a personalized growth goal, upload a classroom video, and reflect on specific moments of instruction using your state or district framework.",
