    "originalNotes": "4.1 Diverse Representation (AF)\t\n\"The product features content and activities that reflect a diverse range of people and cultures as is reasonable given the purpose and content of the lesson.\nLook fors: (a) Examples include a wide variety of people in lay and professional situations; (b) examples are diverse without relying on stereotypes; (c) multiple diversity aspects include gender, race, ethnicity, ability, orientation, socio-economic backgrounds, religion, body type, immigration status, and/or nationality.\"\t\n\nLink to video:\nMeeting the Needs of Diverse Learners Clip\n\n\n",
