    "confidenceReason": "No proposed correction to rate.",
    "originalNotes": "4.2 Empathy Opportunity (AF)\nThe product provides helpful cues to support the development of empathy building and constructive communication when there are diverse perspectives.\nLook fors: (a) Content and activities encourage educators to “put yourself in the shoes” of others; (b) content and activities facilitate perspective-taking (“windows”) and self-reflection (“mirrors”) to explore differences; (c) the product generally encourages an asset-based perspective (considering people’s differences as strengths) rather than focusing on differences as deficits.\n\t\n\nLink to video:\nBeing Honest with Students About Your Own Disabilities \n\n",
    "revisedNotes": "4.2 Empathy Opportunity (AF)\nThe product provides helpful cues to support the development of empathy building and constructive communication when there are diverse perspectives.\nLook fors: (a) Content and activities encourage educators to “put yourself in the shoes” of others; (b) content and activities facilitate perspective-taking (“windows”) and self-reflection (“mirrors”) to explore differences; (c) the product generally encourages an asset-based perspective (considering people’s differences as strengths) rather than focusing on differences as deficits.\n\t\n\nLink to video:\nBeing Honest with Students About Your Own Disabilities \n\n",
    "originalText": "4.2 Empathy Opportunity\nThe video library includes many examples of teachers building empathy and constructive communication through morning meetings, community circles, and classroom discussions. Teachers model perspective-taking by encouraging students to consider others’ experiences and viewpoints, reflect on their own perspectives, and recognize how differences can strengthen the classroom community. These examples promote an asset-based approach that values students’ diverse experiences and perspectives.\nThought Starters that encourage conversation and reflection about the video content ",
    "revisedText": "4.2 Empathy Opportunity\n\nThe video library includes many examples of teachers building empathy and constructive communication through morning meetings, community circles, and classroom discussions. Teachers model perspective-taking by encouraging students to consider others’ experiences and viewpoints, reflect on their own perspectives, and recognize how differences can strengthen the classroom community. These examples promote an asset-based approach that values students’ diverse experiences and perspectives.\nThought Starters that encourage conversation and reflection about the video content ",
