    "originalNotes": "",
    "revisedNotes": "",
    "originalText": "2.1.a Learner: Set Professional Goals\nTeaching Channel’s video coaching and reflection tools help educators set professional learning goals, apply new instructional practices, and reflect on their effectiveness. Educators can upload videos of their instruction, reflect on specific areas of practice, and receive time-stamped feedback aligned to their goals and instructional framework. This ongoing cycle allows educators to revisit their goals, monitor growth, and identify next steps for continued improvement.\nWhen educators upload a video, they can describe the lesson, identify specific areas of focus, and set professional learning goals to guide their reflection and growth.\nEducators can use the Add Link/Upload File feature to share their professional learning goals with colleagues, coaches, or administrators when submitting their video for feedback.",
    "revisedText": "2.1.a Learner: Set Professional Goals\n\nTeaching Channel’s video coaching and reflection tools help educators set professional learning goals, apply new instructional practices, and reflect on their effectiveness. Educators can upload videos of their instruction, reflect on specific areas of practice, and receive time-stamped feedback aligned to their goals and instructional framework. This ongoing cycle allows educators to revisit their goals, monitor growth, and identify next steps for continued improvement.\n\nWhen educators upload a video, they can describe the lesson, identify specific areas of focus, and set professional learning goals to guide their reflection and growth.\nEducators can use the Add Link/Upload File feature to share their professional learning goals with colleagues, coaches, or administrators when submitting their video for feedback.",
