    "revisedNotes": "2.2 Leader Educators seek opportunities for leadership to support student empowerment and success and to improve teaching and learning. (AF)\n2.2.c Model Digital Tool Use Educators model for colleagues the identification, exploration, evaluation, curation and adoption of new digital resources and tools for learning.\nLink to 2.2.c video \n",
    "originalText": "2.2.c Leader: Model Digital Tool Use\nThe platform provides educators with opportunities to model effective technology use in their own practice. By recording and sharing their teaching, educators demonstrate how digital tools can be intentionally integrated into instruction while creating transparency around their decisions and actions. This process allows educators to explain their instructional choices, experiment with new approaches, collect evidence, and reflect on their effectiveness. Rubric-based feedback helps connect these reflections to instructional goals and evaluations, while collaboration with coaches and colleagues provides opportunities for ongoing improvement. Ultimately, this cycle of modeling, reflection, and feedback supports stronger teaching practices and more meaningful technology use that can positively impact student learning.",
    "revisedText": "2.2.c Leader: Model Digital Tool Use\nThe platform provides educators with opportunities to model effective technology use in their own practice. By recording and sharing their teaching, educators demonstrate how digital tools can be intentionally integrated into instruction while creating transparency around their decisions and actions. This process allows educators to explain their instructional choices, experiment with new approaches, collect evidence, and reflect on their effectiveness. Rubric-based feedback helps connect these reflections to instructional goals and evaluations, while collaboration with coaches and colleagues provides opportunities for ongoing improvement. Ultimately, this cycle of modeling, reflection, and feedback supports stronger teaching practices and more meaningful technology use that can positively impact student learning.",
