    "originalText": "2.7.b  Use Technology to Create Assessments\nTeaching Channel provides authentic classroom videos and Thought Starters that demonstrate how educators use technology to design and implement formative and summative assessments. Educators can explore these examples to plan assessments that address learner needs, provide timely feedback, and use evidence of student learning to inform instruction. \nTechnology-Supported Formative Assessment\nSee how educators use digital tools to gather evidence of student understanding, provide opportunities for response, and use that information to guide instruction. \nThe video demonstrates how the teacher enhances assessments for vocabulary and literary understanding using technology tools. Students use digital tools to show comprehension, creativity, and engagement, allowing the teacher to provide prompt feedback.",
    "revisedText": "2.7.b  Use Technology to Create Assessments\nTeaching Channel provides authentic classroom videos and Thought Starters that demonstrate how educators use technology to design and implement formative and summative assessments. Educators can explore these examples to plan assessments that address learner needs, provide timely feedback, and use evidence of student learning to inform instruction. \nTechnology-Supported Formative Assessment\nSee how educators use digital tools to gather evidence of student understanding, provide opportunities for response, and use that information to guide instruction. \n\n\n\n\nThe video demonstrates how the teacher enhances assessments for vocabulary and literary understanding using technology tools. Students use digital tools to show comprehension, creativity, and engagement, allowing the teacher to provide prompt feedback.",
